<title>USA: Phillips unit to raise Soltex asphalt output.</title>
<headline>Phillips unit to raise Soltex asphalt output.</headline>
<dateline>BARTLESVILLE, Okla. 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phillips Petroleum Co said it plans to boost production of its Soltex drilling fluid additive by 40 percent at the Conroe, Texas plant run by Phillips' Drilling Specialists Co unit.</p>
<p>The financial terms of the plant's expansion to boost output were undisclosed, but the project is expected to be completed in the third quarter, Phillips said.</p>
<p>Soltex is a modified asphalt widely used in drilling operations to increase the integrity of the well bore.</p>
</text>
